{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ויאמר, חרטומים</b> — These are the scholars of generation [natural philosophy], who know the principles and the origins of everything, and all deeds done in secret. And so it is written concerning the hartumim of Egypt." "<b>ואשפים</b> — These are the physicians and sorcerers. They are those who alter the nature of a thing for the appearance of the eye." "<b>והכשדים</b> — These are the scholars of the constellations, and the gazrin are the masters of charms who go out to meet serpents. These are the ones the king needs — not the scholars of measures and calculation and proportions and the wisdom of constructions and the supernal wisdom. Now he called to the hartumim, for they know the principle of dreams and how the soul sees visions of the night. He also called to the ashaps, for they know by the pulse of the arm or by the urine the changes of the body, and most dreams follow the disposition of the body. He also called the sorcerers, for they know the hours suited to perform their deeds, that perhaps they may observe and know what the dream is according to the arrangement of the stars at that hour. He also called to the Kasdim, for they know future things according to their craft, by their knowledge of human births, to apply the ascendants on the boundaries and on the aspects of the ministering stars and the two luminaries and the turn of the year and the month and the week and the day. And they knew the birth-moment of Nebuchadnezzar; therefore the Kasdim answered first, for the matter depends on them and on their wisdom according to their words."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase חכמי התולדת literally means 'scholars of generation/nature'; I render it as 'scholars of generation' with the bracketed gloss to preserve the technical medieval term."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:05.391351858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}